  "id": "drug-metabolism",
  "term": "drug metabolism",
  "definition": "Drug metabolism is the body’s processing of a medication, especially in the liver, which can change how effective it is and how toxic it becomes. By turning a drug into other compounds, metabolism can lower or raise risks such as harmful side effects, including effects that depend on drug–drug interactions.",
